        <mxCell id="dsBOZooT3HV5yYKuVwKU-3" value="&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;*: Clocks are determined by m_clk: lr_clk=m_clk/256, s_clk=lr_clk*64&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;**: conv_out is 38 bits because you are adding fourty-eight 32-bit numbers&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;***: 2.25 million multiplies per second required, as such multiplier cannot exceed 12/2.25=5 clock cycles per operation.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Perhaps a more useful way to view this is as follows: we need 1 convolution every lr_clk cycle, thus, we have 256 m_clk cycles to finish the operation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;****: clog2(48 samples) = 6 bits&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
